<section id="faq"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Good to know</div><h2 class="section-title">Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do you have a walk-in shop?</summary><p>No walk-in storefront. Tech Revive provides scheduled drop-off repairs in St. Joseph. We share the agreed drop-off location privately after confirming your appointment.</p></details><details><summary>Can you come to me for a repair?</summary><p>Mobile repair may be available for eligible devices, depending on distance, schedule, and safe working conditions. We confirm any additional travel fee before you book.</p></details><details><summary>How long does a screen repair take?</summary><p>Many standard front-screen repairs take around 30 minutes once the correct part is on hand. Some repairs take longer, and we will give you a realistic estimate for your phone.</p></details><details><summary>Do you keep every screen in stock?</summary><p>No. We generally order the correct part for your specific phone. We'll confirm the estimated delivery time before ordering.</p></details><details><summary>Is a deposit required?</summary><p>For special-order parts, a deposit may be required and goes toward your repair total. We'll explain the amount and cancellation/refund terms before you pay.</p></details><details><summary>What if I have phone insurance?</summary><p>We recommend checking your deductible and coverage first. Your insurance option may be less expensive depending on your plan.</p></details><details><summary>Will my phone be waterproof after a repair?</summary><p>We cannot guarantee the original factory water resistance after a phone has been opened.</p></details><details><summary>Are your screens genuine Apple parts?</summary><p>Our standard replacement options may be aftermarket parts. We'll explain the selected grade, compatibility, and any known feature limitations before you approve the repair.</p></details></div></div></section></main>
